 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N)$, where $N$ is the number of primitives. Each primitive is processed independently with constant-time arithmetic operations [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$ auxiliary space, excluding the input primitive storage [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths:** Camera-independent, allowing for offline analysis of clipping operators without rendering [S1, unofficial]. Provides a ground-truth geometric error metric that isolates clipping logic from renderer artifacts [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations:** Does not account for image-space perceptual quality or reconstruction errors from the splatting process itself [S1, unofficial]. Requires access to the full primitive geometry and covariance [S1, unofficial].
-*   **When to use:** When comparing the geometric fidelity of different half-space clipping algorithms (e.g., XClipGS vs. HC vs. MM) in a controlled, renderer-agnostic manner [S1, unofficial].
-*   **When not to use:** When image-space quality (SSIM, PSNR) or end-user perceptual error is the primary concern; use CDE or Sb in that case [S1, unofficial].
